cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TEMPO (Tracking, Engagement, Messaging & Participant Outreach): automated survey scheduling and participant messaging for longitudinal studies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zweben
    given-names: Danny
    affiliation: Temple University
repository-code: "https://github.com/dzweben/tempo"
url: "https://dzweben.github.io/tempo/"
abstract: >-
  A self-hosted server for research studies that send scheduled surveys and
  reminders. TEMPO integrates a survey database of record with SMS and email
  providers and turns a declarative timeline of study messages into precisely
  timed, auditable outreach: momentary-assessment prompt grids, recurring
  survey cycles with conditional follow-up cadences, visit and compensation
  reminders, and just-in-time personal survey links. It includes a coordinator
  dashboard for completion tracking and a daily reconciliation audit, and a
  delivery path designed for at-most-once guarantees under real-world failure.
keywords:
  - ecological momentary assessment
  - REDCap
  - research software
  - participant management
  - longitudinal studies
  - SMS
  - survey automation
  - clinical research informatics
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22925367
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
